{"duration_api_ms":41293,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"45824e87-e993-4909-9122-079deb0ac2c8","total_cost_usd":0.20291579999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12002,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":5330,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2102},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12002,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5330,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12002},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5330,"cacheReadInputTokens":1459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12002,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.20291579999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2102,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"merged_document\":\"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets. It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can later be used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\n\\nThis BIP falls under the GPL License.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence can be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription. It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the mnemonic\\n\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. More entropy improves security but increases the sentence length. The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, these numbers are converted into words, and the joined words are used as the mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\"decisions\":[],\"dispositions\":[{\"segment\":\"a3\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"reason\":\"Abstract: corrected letters to words and UTOXs to wallets.\"},{\"segment\":\"a4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"reason\":\"Abstract: BIP 39 produces a binary seed, not an ASCII seed.\"},{\"segment\":\"a5\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This seed can later be used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\",\"reason\":\"Abstract: word order smoothed.\"},{\"segment\":\"a9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: satoshis corrected to seed.\"},{\"segment\":\"a10\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The sentence can be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: present tense.\"},{\"segment\":\"a11\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: determinism corrected to randomness.\"},{\"segment\":\"a12\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Motivation: typo süeed fixed, contraction expanded.\"},{\"segment\":\"b1\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"## Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"Section heading: typo memonic fixed.\"},{\"segment\":\"b2\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: demonic typo fixed; 23 corrected to 32.\"},{\"segment\":\"b3\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"More entropy improves security but increases the sentence length.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: tightened wording.\"},{\"segment\":\"b4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: general voice instead of we.\"},{\"segment\":\"b5\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: 1024-2048 byts corrected to 128-256 bits.\"},{\"segment\":\"b7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: SHA652 corrected to SHA256.\"},{\"segment\":\"b8\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: checksum is appended at the end, not the start.\"},{\"segment\":\"b9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: 12 bits corrected to 11 bits.\"},{\"segment\":\"b10\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Finally, these numbers are converted into words, and the joined words are used as the mnemonic sentence.\",\"reason\":\"Generating: general voice instead of we.\"}],\"mismatch\":\"\",\"additions\":[{\"statement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"corrects\":\"a group of easy to remember letters -- for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Abstract (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"BIP 39 mnemonics are word lists used for deterministic wallets.\"},{\"statement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"corrects\":\"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Abstract (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"BIP 39 derives a 512-bit binary seed via PBKDF2.\"},{\"statement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"corrects\":\"representations of a wallet satoshis\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Motivation (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"The mnemonic represents a wallet seed, not satoshis.\"},{\"statement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"corrects\":\"computer-generated determinism\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Motivation (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"The mnemonic transcribes random entropy.\"},{\"statement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"a multiple of 23 bits\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"CS = ENT / 32 in the table requires ENT divisible by 32.\"},{\"statement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"1024-2048 byts\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"The document's own table spans ENT 128 to 256 bits.\"},{\"statement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"corrects\":\"SHA652 hash\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"SHA652 does not exist; BIP 39 uses SHA256.\"},{\"statement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"corrects\":\"appended to the start of the initial entropy\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"Appending places the checksum at the end of the entropy.\"},{\"statement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"corrects\":\"groups of 12 bits\",\"basis\":\"citation\",\"source\":\"BIP 39, Generating the mnemonic (bitcoin/bips repository, bip-0039.mediawiki)\",\"reason\":\"0-2047 is 11 bits, and the table divides by 11.\"}]}","ttft_ms":20065,"type":"result","duration_ms":41361,"uuid":"f6170133-5a46-4b0d-9e65-11d9de834ccc","ttft_stream_ms":1305,"time_to_request_ms":114,"first_content_frame_ms":1306,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
